</version></versions></category></categories><variable id="b9bd1abb-0f2b-40c1-bdf9-53328a1810c4" name="lperc_info" type="0"><notes><versions><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="0"><property name="5@note1" value="------------------------" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="1"><property name="5@note2" value=" labels" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="2"><property name="5@note3" value="========================" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF></versions><property name="5@note1" value="------------------------" type="8" context="Question"/><property name="5@note2" value=" labels" type="8" context="Question"/><property name="5@note3" value="========================" type="8" context="Question"/></notes><labels context="LABEL"><versions><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="0"><text context="QUESTION" xml:lang="en-US">%</text></DIFF></versions><text context="QUESTION" xml:lang="en-US">%</text></labels><versions><version name="32"><variable name="lperc_info" type="0"/></version></versions></variable><variable id="3860f6d3-e3d5-4900-ac77-94e9b2c86003" name="Hello" type="0"><templates><versions><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="0"><property name="Question" value="question.htm" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF></versions><property name="Question" value="question.htm" type="8" context="Question"/></templates><notes><versions><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="0"><property name="5@note1" value="------------------------" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="1"><property name="5@note2" value=" Instructions" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="2"><property name="5@note3" value="========================" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF><DIFF OP="DEL" name="105" Index="0"/><DIFF OP="DEL" name="105" Index="0"/><DIFF OP="DEL" name="105" Index="0"/></versions></notes><labels context="LABEL"><versions><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="0"><text context="QUESTION" xml:lang="en-US">&lt;p&gt;While this can be consider an example of a basic information question, it is actually possible to create a lot of content in a single question.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It is advised that content is wrapped in paragraph tags because this creates natural spacing between each paragraph&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;it is also possible to use html tags such as numbered and unordered list tags.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;To demonstrate the different in which you can apply formatting to different parts of the content, the following is an unordered list&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;This is an exmaple of &lt;span class='bold'&gt;bold&lt;/span&gt; text.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Two levels of bold are provided &lt;span class='ltbold'&gt;light bold&lt;/span&gt; and &lt;span class='bold'&gt;bold as shown above&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;This TEXT is typed in all caps and this &lt;span class='caps'&gt;text&lt;/span&gt; is formatted as all caps.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Text can also be &lt;span class='underline'&gt;underlined&lt;/span&gt; or &lt;span class='italic'&gt;italicised&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;We are also playing with the idea of allowing you deliver &lt;span class='plusfour'&gt;impact&lt;/span&gt; by increasing the font size by four points &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Finally, we are looking at whether its possible to provide superscript such as 13m&lt;span class='sup minusfour'&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; and subscript such as H&lt;span class='sub minusfour'&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;O&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Its also possible to create content through banners, the question template defines where these banners appear.  In this example we have placed the banners below the question label, but this is just for demonstration purposes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a quick test, the word &lt;b&gt;fox&lt;/b&gt; has been bolded using html tags. This is the old method and should not be used, but we want to be user that the introduction of line breaks is &lt;i&gt;resolved&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</text></DIFF><DIFF OP="DEL" name="78" Index="0"/><DIFF OP="ADD" name="78" Index="0"><text context="QUESTION" xml:lang="en-US">&lt;p&gt;While this can be consider an example of a basic information question, it is actually possible to create a lot of content in a single question.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It is advised that content is wrapped in paragraph tags because this creates natural spacing between each paragraph&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;it is also possible to use html tags such as numbered and unordered list tags.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;To demonstrate the different in which you can apply formatting to different parts of the content, the following is an unordered list&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;This is an exmaple of &lt;span class='bold'&gt;bold&lt;/span&gt; text.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Two levels of bold are provided &lt;span class='ltbold'&gt;light bold&lt;/span&gt; and &lt;span class='bold'&gt;bold as shown above&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;This TEXT is typed in all caps and this &lt;span class='caps'&gt;text&lt;/span&gt; is formatted as all caps.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Text can also be &lt;span class='underline'&gt;underlined&lt;/span&gt; or &lt;span class='italic'&gt;italicised&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;We are also playing with the idea of allowing you deliver &lt;span class='plusfour'&gt;impact&lt;/span&gt; by increasing the font size by four points &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Finally, we are looking at whether its possible to provide superscript such as 13m&lt;span class='sup minusfour'&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; and subscript such as H&lt;span class='sub minusfour'&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;O&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Its also possible to create content through banners, the question template defines where these banners appear.  In this example we have placed the banners below the question label, but this is just for demonstration purposes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a quick test, the word &lt;b&gt;fox&lt;/b&gt; has been bolded using html tags. This is the old method and should not be used, but we want to be user that the introduction of line breaks is &lt;i&gt;resolved&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For more information click &lt;a href='https:\\ipsos.com' target='_blank'&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</text></DIFF></versions><text context="QUESTION" xml:lang="en-US">&lt;p&gt;While this can be consider an example of a basic information question, it is actually possible to create a lot of content in a single question.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It is advised that content is wrapped in paragraph tags because this creates natural spacing between each paragraph&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;it is also possible to use html tags such as numbered and unordered list tags.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;To demonstrate the different in which you can apply formatting to different parts of the content, the following is an unordered list&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;This is an exmaple of &lt;span class='bold'&gt;bold&lt;/span&gt; text.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Two levels of bold are provided &lt;span class='ltbold'&gt;light bold&lt;/span&gt; and &lt;span class='bold'&gt;bold as shown above&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;This TEXT is typed in all caps and this &lt;span class='caps'&gt;text&lt;/span&gt; is formatted as all caps.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Text can also be &lt;span class='underline'&gt;underlined&lt;/span&gt; or &lt;span class='italic'&gt;italicised&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;We are also playing with the idea of allowing you deliver &lt;span class='plusfour'&gt;impact&lt;/span&gt; by increasing the font size by four points &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Finally, we are looking at whether its possible to provide superscript such as 13m&lt;span class='sup minusfour'&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; and subscript such as H&lt;span class='sub minusfour'&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;O&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Its also possible to create content through banners, the question template defines where these banners appear.  In this example we have placed the banners below the question label, but this is just for demonstration purposes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a quick test, the word &lt;b&gt;fox&lt;/b&gt; has been bolded using html tags. This is the old method and should not be used, but we want to be user that the introduction of line breaks is &lt;i&gt;resolved&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For more information click &lt;a href='https:\\ipsos.com' target='_blank'&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</text></labels><versions><version name="32"><variable name="Hello" type="0"/></version></versions><properties><versions><DIFF OP="ADD" name="44" Index="0"><property name="CurrentTab" value="Presenting" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF><DIFF OP="DEL" name="105" Index="0"/><DIFF OP="ADD" name="105" Index="0"><property name="CurrentTab" value="Information" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF></versions><property name="CurrentTab" value="Information" type="8" context="Question"/></properties></variable><variable id="268de879-370c-4136-bf58-bcdb976f316f" name="QuestionStructure1" type="2" max="100" maxtype="3"><styles><versions><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="0"><property name="BgColor" value="singleline:" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="1"><property name="Width" value="50%" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF></versions><property name="BgColor" value="singleline:" type="8" context="Question"/><property name="Width" value="50%" type="8" context="Question"/></styles><templates><versions><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="0"><property name="Question" value="question.htm" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF></versions><property name="Question" value="question.htm" type="8" context="Question"/></templates><notes><versions><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="0"><property name="5@note1" value="----------------------" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="1"><property name="5@note2" value=" SingleLine - text" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF><DIFF OP="ADD" name="32" Index="2"><property name="5@note3" value="======================" type="8" context="Question"/></DIFF></